Permission and attribution

You may use, adapt, reproduce, redistribute and commercially use the covered
XUI design, provided you give readable attribution containing exactly:

XUI (xxx client)

Include IMDelewer and a link to the original source when practical. Attribution
must be accessible to an ordinary user or reader:

- For an open-source client, include it in the repository README or in an
  in-game About/Credits page.
- For a closed-source client, include it in an in-game About/Credits page or
  another accessible credits screen distributed with the client.
- For a published design or mockup, include it with that publication.

A suitable credit is:

Interface design based on XUI (xxx client), by IMDelewer.

This condition applies when covered visual expression is copied from source,
recreated from screenshots or video, ported to another framework, or reproduced
with newly written code. Rewriting the implementation does not remove the
attribution condition for reproducing the covered design. Keep this license
with distributions of the covered design materials. Mark changes and do not
claim endorsement by IMDelewer.

Inspiration and general ideas

The project's attribution policy also asks you to credit XUI when it inspired
your interface. Please do this even if you wrote every line yourself.
The legally binding permission above concerns protected expression only;
it does not assert ownership of general ideas, standard controls, glass
materials, common layouts, independent designs, or anything outside the
rights granted by applicable law. Mere inspiration by an unprotected idea
is a request for acknowledgment, not a claim of exclusive rights.

